{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"agent_message","text":"The problem is fixed and I submitted the mitigation. The submission endpoint returned `{\"status\":\"200\",\"message\":\"Submission received\",\"stage\":\"mitigation\"}`.\n\n**Root cause:** The `search` pods carried the label `service-route=frontend`, which is the selector of the `frontend` Service. About half of the requests to `frontend:5000` therefore went to the `search` pod, which doesn't listen on that port. Those requests failed with connection errors.\n\n**Fix:** I removed the `service-route` label from the `search` deployment's pod template. The `frontend` endpoints now list only the real frontend pod. Eight test requests to `/hotels` all returned 200 in about 3 ms, where before roughly half had failed.\n\nI didn't check traces or metrics. I found this from the pod labels and the Service endpoints."}}
